cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite both the software and
  the accompanying article.
title: >-
  DEVS_simulation_framework: a DEVS-based simulation framework for evaluating
  path planning algorithms in autonomous mobile robot operations
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/minhochoe66/DEVS_simulation_framework"
abstract: >-
  A discrete event system specification (DEVS) simulation framework that
  evaluates global and local path planning algorithms for autonomous mobile
  robots consistently, from a single robot to a multi-robot fleet operation.
  Perception, planning, maneuvering, fleet management, scheduling and equipment
  operation are represented as coupled discrete-event models, and a unified
  planner interface allows global and local algorithms to be replaced without
  modifying the surrounding models.
keywords:
  - autonomous mobile robot
  - path planning
  - discrete event system specification
  - discrete-event simulation
  - performance evaluation
  - fleet operation
